codex
The entry residual shows the loop summary is being used, but the recursive alphabet precondition is forcing symbolic strings into concrete-length constructor branches and making the backend expand the specification itself. The theorem does not need that restriction: proving all modeled `IntSeq` strings of length 1–100 is stronger than the prompt’s letters-and-spaces subset. I’m removing only that narrowing precondition and its unused helper.
